Drop O_EXCL from the image open under Cosmopolitan.

mke2fs sets EXT2_FLAG_EXCLUSIVE unconditionally, so unix_open() adds O_EXCL
to the image open. On a regular file without O_CREAT that is a no-op on
Linux, but cosmo's NT open() rejects it with EINVAL ("...while setting up
superblock"). O_EXCL only matters for block devices, which a Windows image
is not; this file only, since O_CREAT|O_EXCL is relied on elsewhere.

--- a/lib/ext2fs/unix_io.c
+++ b/lib/ext2fs/unix_io.c
@@ -39,6 +39,10 @@
 #include <errno.h>
 #endif
 #include <fcntl.h>
+#ifdef __COSMOPOLITAN__
+#undef O_EXCL
+#define O_EXCL 0
+#endif
 #include <time.h>
 #ifdef __linux__
 #include <sys/utsname.h>
